Name: zeroskip_index_path
Type: STRING
Default-Value: NULL
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

The directory under which the zeroskip backend caches pointer tables, which
speed up opening a database that has accumulated unordered files.  Each
database gets its own subdirectory beneath this path.  If not specified,
the cache lives in a zeroskip.cache directory inside each database instead.

A tmpfs is a good choice: the cache is a pure optimisation, and losing it
costs only time.  It must not be the directory of any database, and it must
not be writable by untrusted users -- a planted table yields wrong records,
which is why the default stays inside the database directory rather than
somewhere shared.
